{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 14:44:18", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a9c3efc3-594d-49a4-b8b5-e5c99326c765', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "task": "Compare TDD Coordinator performance between haiku and sonnet models",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation",\n  "test_scenarios": [\n    {\n      "complexity": "low",\n      "description": "Simple component creation"\n    },\n    {\n      "complexity": "medium",\n      "description": "Form validation and state management"\n    },\n    {\n      "complexity": "high",\n      "description": "Complex state synchronization and error handling"\n    }\n  ],\n  "comparison_metrics": [\n    "test coverage",\n    "code quality",\n    "cycle completion time",\n    "error reduction"\n  ]\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RRMMx6GyDYZCHCq4QqTyrf', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RRMMx6GyDYZCHCq4QqTyrf', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation Requirements\\n\\n## Objective\\nCompare performance of claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929 against current claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 model\\n\\n## Comparison Metrics\\n1. Test Coverage\\n2. Code Quality\\n3. TDD Cycle Completion Time\\n4. Error Reduction Rate\\n\\n## Test Scenarios\\n1. Low Complexity: Simple component creation\\n2. Medium Complexity: Form validation and state management\\n3. High Complexity: Complex state synchronization and error handling\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- Demonstrate +50% improvement in success rate\\n- Verify consistent performance across complexity levels\\n- Validate code quality metrics improve"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016Ec2HMoqusmv3wHRmUBAYH', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation', 'description': 'Compare TDD Coordinator performance between haiku and sonnet models across three complexity levels using test coverage, code quality, cycle completion time, and error reduction metrics'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016Ec2HMoqusmv3wHRmUBAYH', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "a24b246e", "message": "Created project: TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation", "summary": {"project_id": "a24b246e", "project_name": "TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation", "description": "Compare TDD Coordinator performance between haiku and sonnet models across three complexity levels using test coverage, code quality, cycle completion time, and error reduction metrics", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T14:41:25.092812", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T14:41:25.092812", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T14:41:25.092812", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QsCa2svMYCxBuaVJVp92fb', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nCompare performance of claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022 against claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 models in the TDD Coordinator role across three complexity levels.\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Demonstrate +50% improvement in success rate\n- Verify consistent performance across complexity levels  \n- Validate code quality metrics improve\n\n## Milestone 1: Test Framework Setup and Haiku Baseline\n**Duration**: 1 week\n**Objective**: Establish testing framework and capture haiku model baseline performance\n\n### Deliverables:\n- Test harness for automated TDD Coordinator evaluation\n- Standardized test scenarios (low, medium, high complexity)\n- Baseline metrics for haiku model across all scenarios\n- Performance measurement tools\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Test framework can execute all 3 complexity scenarios\n- Baseline metrics captured for haiku model: test coverage, code quality, cycle time, error rate\n- Repeatable test execution process established\n\n### Dependencies: None\n\n## Milestone 2: Sonnet Model Performance Evaluation  \n**Duration**: 1 week\n**Objective**: Execute identical test scenarios with sonnet model and capture performance metrics\n\n### Deliverables:\n- Complete sonnet model performance data\n- Comparative analysis framework\n- Initial performance comparison results\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Identical test scenarios executed with sonnet model\n- Performance metrics captured using same measurement tools\n- Data ready for comparative analysis\n\n### Dependencies: Milestone 1 complete\n\n## Milestone 3: Performance Analysis and Reporting\n**Duration**: 0.5 weeks  \n**Objective**: Analyze comparative results and generate comprehensive performance report\n\n### Deliverables:\n- Detailed performance comparison report\n- Recommendations for model selection\n- Documentation of findings and methodologies\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Quantitative comparison across all 4 metrics\n- Clear recommendation on model performance\n- Reproducible methodology documented\n- Success criteria validation (50% improvement target)\n\n### Dependencies: Milestone 2 complete\n\n## Total Timeline: 2.5 weeks'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QsCa2svMYCxBuaVJVp92fb', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_144136.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_144136.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01YbnigBNbLjwgAYFxumpuZL', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'project_scope': 'TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation comparing haiku vs sonnet models', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01YbnigBNbLjwgAYFxumpuZL', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TSQGnVVTzRLvzJsqeh9dpb', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TSQGnVVTzRLvzJsqeh9dpb', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: Web UI Background Color Change\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted styling modification** using a **minimal change architecture**. The project requires changing a single CSS property while maintaining system integrity and accessibility.\\n\\n**Pattern**: Configuration-based theming approach\\n**Rationale**: For a simple color change, we use the existing CSS architecture but implement it in a way that\'s maintainable and could support future theming needs.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **CSS**: Direct modification of existing stylesheets\\n- **Build System**: Existing build pipeline (preserved)\\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Maintained through existing setup\\n\\n**Why this approach**:\\n- **CSS over CSS-in-JS**: Requirements specify working with existing `index.css`, so we maintain consistency\\n- **Direct modification over theming framework**: Overkill for single color change, but we\'ll structure it to enable future expansion\\n- **Existing build tools**: No need to introduce complexity for a simple change\\n\\n### Testing\\n- **Visual Regression**: Manual browser testing across devices\\n- **Accessibility**: Color contrast validation tools\\n- **Functional**: Ensure no JavaScript or layout breakage\\n\\n**Alternatives considered**:\\n- CSS Variables: Would be ideal for theming but requires more extensive changes\\n- SCSS/CSS Framework: Overkill for current scope but noted for future\\n- Theme switching system: Out of scope but architecture supports future implementation\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. Style Configuration Layer\\n**Responsibility**: Define color values and ensure consistency\\n**Location**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/index.css`\\n**Changes**: Update background-color values\\n\\n### 2. Accessibility Validation Layer\\n**Responsibility**: Ensure color contrast compliance\\n**Implementation**: Testing and validation process\\n**Tools**: WCAG color contrast checkers\\n\\n### 3. Compatibility Verification Layer\\n**Responsibility**: Ensure Bootstrap and existing styles remain functional\\n**Implementation**: Cross-browser testing protocol\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.css                 # PRIMARY TARGET - background color changes\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/               # NO CHANGES (verify compatibility)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 assets/                  # NO CHANGES (verify compatibility)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 [other existing files]   # NO CHANGES (verify compatibility)\\n```\\n\\n**Rationale**: Minimal file impact reduces risk while achieving requirements.\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**N/A** - This is a pure styling change with no data model implications.\\n\\n## CSS Architecture Design\\n\\n### Current State\\n```css\\nbody {\\n  background-color: #1a1d29; /* Current dark blue */\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Proposed State\\n```css\\n/* Option 1: Direct replacement */\\nbody {\\n  background-color: #1a291d; /* Dark green equivalent */\\n}\\n\\n/* Option 2: CSS Custom Properties (Future-proofing) */\\n:root {\\n  --bg-primary: #1a291d;     /* Dark green */\\n  --bg-contrast: #2d4a27;    /* Complementary green if needed */\\n}\\n\\nbody {\\n  background-color: var(--bg-primary);\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Color Strategy\\n**Primary Color**: `#1a291d` (Dark forest green)\\n- Maintains similar brightness to original `#1a1d29`\\n- Preserves accessibility contrast ratios\\n- Provides professional, calming aesthetic\\n\\n**Fallback Strategy**: Test multiple green variants:\\n1. `#1a291d` (Primary choice)\\n2. `#1d2a1a` (Alternative 1)\\n3. `#1f2d1c` (Alternative 2 - slightly lighter)\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Preparation\\n1. **Backup current files**\\n2. **Document current color values**\\n3. **Set up local testing environment**\\n\\n### Phase 2: Color Implementation\\n1. **Update index.css with new background color**\\n2. **Test initial render**\\n3. **Validate no CSS conflicts**\\n\\n### Phase 3: Validation\\n1. **Accessibility testing** (contrast ratios)\\n2. **Cross-browser testing** (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\\n3. **Responsive testing** (mobile, tablet, desktop)\\n4. **Component interaction testing**\\n\\n### Phase 4: Verification\\n1. **Full application walkthrough**\\n2. **Performance impact assessment**\\n3. **Final visual QA**\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n- **Browser Matrix**: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n- **Device Testing**: Desktop (1920x1080), Tablet (768px), Mobile (375px)\\n- **Functionality Check**: Ensure all interactive elements work\\n\\n### Accessibility Testing\\n- **Tool**: WebAIM Color Contrast Checker\\n- **Standard**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\\n- **Validation**: Background vs text color combinations\\n\\n### Regression Testing\\n- **Bootstrap Integration**: Verify no Bootstrap class conflicts\\n- **Component Rendering**: Ensure all components render correctly\\n- **Performance**: Verify no performance degradation\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- **Development**: Local testing environment\\n- **Staging**: Apply changes to staging for validation\\n- **Production**: Deploy after full testing cycle\\n\\n### Rollback Plan\\n1. **Git commit** before changes for easy reversion\\n2. **File backup** of index.css\\n3. **Quick rollback** procedure documented\\n\\n### CI/CD Considerations\\n- **Build verification**: Ensure CSS compiles without errors\\n- **Automated testing**: Run existing test suite to catch regressions\\n- **Deploy verification**: Smoke test after deployment\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: CSS Custom Properties System\\n**Pros**: Future-proof, enables theme switching\\n**Cons**: More complex than requirements need\\n**Decision**: Implement basic version, document for future enhancement\\n\\n### Alternative 2: CSS-in-JS Solution\\n**Pros**: Component-scoped styling, dynamic themes\\n**Cons**: Major architecture change, overkill for single color\\n**Decision**: Rejected for current scope\\n\\n### Alternative 3: SCSS/SASS Implementation\\n**Pros**: Variables, mixins, better organization\\n**Cons**: Adds build complexity, not needed for single change\\n**Decision**: Document for future consideration\\n\\n### Alternative 4: Multiple Theme System\\n**Pros**: User choice, future flexibility\\n**Cons**: Scope creep, complex implementation\\n**Decision**: Out of scope, but architecture supports future addition\\n\\n## Risk Assessment and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Color Contrast Issues\\n**Impact**: Medium - Accessibility compliance failure\\n**Probability**: Low - Pre-validated color choices\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive contrast testing before deployment\\n\\n### Risk 2: Bootstrap Conflicts\\n**Impact**: Medium - Layout or styling breaks\\n**Probability**: Low - Minimal CSS surface area\\n**Mitigation**: Thorough compatibility testing\\n\\n### Risk 3: Browser Compatibility\\n**Impact**: Low - Modern CSS widely supported\\n**Probability**: Very Low - Basic color property\\n**Mitigation**: Multi-browser testing protocol\\n\\n### Risk 4: Performance Impact\\n**Impact**: Very Low - CSS color change minimal cost\\n**Probability**: Very Low - No computational complexity added\\n**Mitigation**: Performance monitoring during testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. **Color Preference**: Do you prefer the suggested `#1a291d` or would you like to see alternatives?\\n2. **Future Theming**: Should we implement CSS custom properties for easier future theme changes?\\n3. **Scope Boundary**: Are you certain only the main background needs to change, or should complementary colors be considered?\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Visual**: Background displays as dark green instead of dark blue\\n2. **Accessibility**: All text maintains WCAG AA contrast ratios\\n3. **Compatibility**: Zero functional regressions\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable performance impact\\n\\n## Future Considerations\\n\\n### Theme System Foundation\\nThis implementation could serve as the foundation for a future theme switching system:\\n- CSS custom properties already documented\\n- Color organization established\\n- Testing protocols proven\\n\\n### Maintainability\\n- Document color choices for future reference\\n- Establish color naming conventions\\n- Create change log for theme modifications\\n\\n## Implementation Timeline\\n\\n1. **Preparation**: 30 minutes\\n2. **Implementation**: 15 minutes\\n3. **Testing**: 2-3 hours (comprehensive)\\n4. **Deployment**: 15 minutes\\n5. **Verification**: 30 minutes\\n\\n**Total Estimated Time**: 3-4 hours for complete, thorough implementation\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture balances the simplicity required by the scope with the maintainability needed for a professional application. The approach minimizes risk while establishing patterns that could support future theming enhancements.\\n\\nThe single-file change strategy ensures minimal impact while comprehensive testing protocols guarantee quality and accessibility compliance."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BRTEK4iG6mNZvvyVPXPSJb', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'project_description': 'TDD Coordinator Model Performance Validation - comparing claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 vs claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022 models across 3 complexity levels with metrics: test coverage, code quality, cycle completion time, error reduction', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BRTEK4iG6mNZvvyVPXPSJb', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Designed a Test-Driven Experimentation Architecture using Node.js/TypeScript with modular experiment framework pattern. The system implements controlled A/B testing between Claude models across three complexity levels, with comprehensive metrics collection and statistical analysis capabilities.", "key_decisions": ["Node.js/TypeScript chosen over Python for superior AI SDK integration and type safety for experiment integrity", "PostgreSQL selected over NoSQL for ACID compliance critical to experiment data consistency", "Modular monolith architecture over microservices to balance maintainability with experiment complexity", "Hybrid real-time/batch processing for experiment monitoring with statistical analysis", "Strategy pattern for model abstraction enabling fair comparison between Claude variants", "Custom metrics collection combined with industry-standard tools (Jest) for TDD-specific validation"], "self_analysis": "The architecture successfully addresses the experimental validation requirements by providing a scientifically rigorous framework for comparing AI models in TDD scenarios. The modular design enables controlled testing while the comprehensive metrics system ensures reliable performance measurement across the four key criteria."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of