{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:42:07", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1fde87f7-5574-4e7d-b169-e3ad1556ffcd', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/requirements.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013xaUoab9UjvoX27akYrnQU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013xaUoab9UjvoX27akYrnQU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Activity Tracking Fixes - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThis project addresses three critical bugs in the Ensemble UI agent system that prevent proper activity tracking. Files generated by agents, request counts, and activity metrics are not being correctly recorded or surfaced via the activity APIs.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe Ensemble UI shows zero files generated and zero agent counts even when agents are actively producing files and completing tasks. This is a **tracking/visibility bug**, not a functionality bug - the agents ARE working correctly, but their activity is not being reported to the UI.\\n\\n### Root Causes Identified\\n\\n1. **Bug #1: WriteFileTool Does Not Record to Activity Tracker** (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/runtime/agents/tools.py` - `WriteFileTool.execute()`\\n   - Impact: Files written by spawned agents are never tracked\\n\\n2. **Bug #2: Request Counts Never Incremented** (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n   - Method `increment_request_counts()` is defined but never called\\n   - Impact: Timeline view shows 0 agents, 0 files, 0 commits for all requests\\n\\n3. **Bug #3: File Tracking Only Scans Output Directory** (LOW PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n   - Only files in output directory are scanned; files elsewhere are missed\\n   - Impact: Test files, source files written outside output directory not tracked\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Primary**: Ensure all file writes by agents are tracked via `record_file_generated()`\\n2. **Secondary**: Auto-increment request counters when agents start, files generate, commits occur\\n3. **Tertiary**: Validate fixes by confirming `/api/activity/files` returns correct data\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Modify `WriteFileTool` to accept and use tracking context (agent_id, request_id, agent_name)\\n- Modify `ToolRegistry.default()` to pass tracking context to WriteFileTool\\n- Add auto-increment calls to `record_agent_started()`, `record_file_generated()`, `record_git_commit()`\\n- Add tests to verify activity tracking works end-to-end\\n- Update existing tests if needed to accommodate new parameters\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the activity API endpoints (they already work correctly)\\n- Changing the frontend display logic (it already consumes the API correctly)\\n- Major refactoring of the tool system architecture\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Fix 1: WriteFileTool Tracking\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(self, agent_definition: Optional[\\"AgentDefinition\\"] = None):\\n        self.agent_definition = agent_definition\\n```\\n\\n**Required Changes:**\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self, \\n        agent_definition: Optional[\\"AgentDefinition\\"] = None,\\n        agent_id: Optional[str] = None,\\n        agent_name: Optional[str] = None,\\n        request_id: Optional[str] = None\\n    ):\\n        self.agent_definition = agent_definition\\n        self.agent_id = agent_id\\n        self.agent_name = agent_name or (agent_definition.name if agent_definition else \\"unknown\\")\\n        self.request_id = request_id\\n```\\n\\n**In execute() method, after successful write:**\\n```python\\nif self.agent_id and self.request_id:\\n    try:\\n        from .runtime import AgentRuntime\\n        activity_tracker = AgentRuntime.get_activity_tracker()\\n        \\n        file_ext = file_path.suffix.lower()\\n        file_type_map = {\\n            \\".md\\": \\"markdown\\", \\".py\\": \\"python\\", \\".js\\": \\"javascript\\",\\n            \\".tsx\\": \\"typescript-react\\", \\".ts\\": \\"typescript\\",\\n            \\".json\\": \\"json\\", \\".yaml\\": \\"yaml\\", \\".yml\\": \\"yaml\\", \\".txt\\": \\"text\\"\\n        }\\n        file_type = file_type_map.get(file_ext, \\"unknown\\")\\n        \\n        preview = content[:500] if len(content) > 500 else content\\n        \\n        activity_tracker.record_file_generated(\\n            agent_id=self.agent_id,\\n            agent_name=self.agent_name,\\n            request_id=self.request_id,\\n            file_path=str(file_path),\\n            file_size=len(content),\\n            file_type=file_type,\\n            preview=preview\\n        )\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        logger.warning(f\\"Failed to record file generation: {e}\\")\\n```\\n\\n### Fix 2: ToolRegistry.default() Update\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n```python\\nregistry.register(WriteFileTool(agent_definition))\\n```\\n\\n**Required Change:**\\n```python\\nregistry.register(WriteFileTool(\\n    agent_definition=agent_definition,\\n    agent_id=agent_id,\\n    agent_name=agent_definition.name if agent_definition else None,\\n    request_id=request_id\\n))\\n```\\n\\n### Fix 3: Auto-Increment Request Counts\\n\\n**In `record_agent_started()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_started(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, agents=1)\\n```\\n\\n**In `record_file_generated()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_file_generated(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, files=1)\\n```\\n\\n**In `record_git_commit()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_git_commit(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, commits=1)\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **File Tracking Verification:**\\n   - Run an agent workflow that creates files\\n   - Query `/api/activity/files` \\n   - Verify response includes newly created files with correct metadata\\n\\n2. **Request Counts Verification:**\\n   - Query `/api/activity/timeline`\\n   - Verify `agent_count`, `file_count`, `commit_count` are non-zero for active requests\\n\\n3. **Regression Testing:**\\n   - All existing tests pass\\n   - New tests for activity tracking pass\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n\\n1. **Unit Tests:**\\n   - Test WriteFileTool records to activity tracker when context is provided\\n   - Test WriteFileTool gracefully handles missing context (backward compatibility)\\n   - Test increment_request_counts updates counters correctly\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests:**\\n   - Test full agent execution records file generation\\n   - Test timeline API returns correct counts\\n   - Test files API returns files with correct agent attribution\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n\\n1. The ActivityTracker singleton pattern will work for capturing all file writes\\n2. Import cycle concerns can be handled with local imports\\n3. Existing API endpoints don\'t need modification - they already query the tracker correctly\\n4. Minor performance impact of tracking is acceptable\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n1. Must maintain backward compatibility - tools should work even without tracking context\\n2. Must not break existing tests\\n3. Changes should be localized to the identified files\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `src/runtime/agents/tools.py` with WriteFileTool tracking\\n2. Updated `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` with auto-increment calls\\n3. Test file(s) verifying the fix\\n4. Updated documentation (this file + any inline comments)\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Requirements documented: 2026-01-14*\\n*Project ID: 87cc4aaf*\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Fjpiv5od2E6SucVEuNTnuy', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Activity Tracking Fixes', 'description': 'Implement fixes for activity tracking in Ensemble UI agent system, addressing file tracking, request counts, and visibility issues'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Fjpiv5od2E6SucVEuNTnuy', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "2c8495a2", "message": "Created project: Activity Tracking Fixes", "summary": {"project_id": "2c8495a2", "project_name": "Activity Tracking Fixes", "description": "Implement fixes for activity tracking in Ensemble UI agent system, addressing file tracking, request counts, and visibility issues", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:04.206217", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:04.206217", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:42:04.206217", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Activity Tracking Fixes\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018cCqXowfRV4ZfrEPh8F1hy', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '2c8495a2', 'description': 'Implement activity tracking fixes as specified in requirements document', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018cCqXowfRV4ZfrEPh8F1hy', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "3664c143", "message": "Added task: Implement activity tracking fixes as specified in requirements document"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id":