514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502\\n       \\u2502 returns            \\u2502 records            \\u2502 sets status        \\u2502 shows\\n       \\u2502 needs_user_input   \\u2502 question           \\u2502 to \\"completed\\"     \\u2502 \\"completed\\"\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502 correctly          \\u2502 (WRONG!)           \\u2502 (WRONG!)\\n       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2534\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2534\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                                   \\u2717 PIPELINE ENDS\\n```\\n\\n## Target Architecture (Fixed Flow)\\n\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510      \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510      \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510      \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502   Agent     \\u2502      \\u2502   Runtime   \\u2502      \\u2502   Backend   \\u2502      \\u2502     UI      \\u2502\\n\\u2502  (ED)       \\u2502\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25b6\\u2502  Execute    \\u2502\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25b6\\u2502 Background  \\u2502\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25b6\\u2502  Display    \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518      \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518      \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518      \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502\\n       \\u2502 returns            \\u2502 records            \\u2502 sets status to     \\u2502 shows\\n       \\u2502 needs_user_input   \\u2502 question           \\u2502 \\"awaiting_user_    \\u2502 \\"waiting\\"\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502 correctly          \\u2502 input\\" + stores    \\u2502 badge\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502 context            \\u2502\\n       \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502                    \\u2502\\n       \\u25bc                    \\u2502                    \\u25bc                    \\u25bc\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510             \\u2502            \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510      \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502 User        \\u2502             \\u2502            \\u2502 Backend     \\u2502      \\u2502 UI shows    \\u2502\\n\\u2502 sees        \\u2502\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2534\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25b6\\u2502 receives    \\u2502\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25b6\\u2502 agent       \\u2502\\n\\u2502 question    \\u2502                          \\u2502 answer      \\u2502      \\u2502 running     \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518                          \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518      \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                                                \\u2502\\n                                                \\u25bc\\n                                         \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n                                         \\u2502 Spawn new   \\u2502\\n                                         \\u2502 agent with  \\u2502\\n                                         \\u2502 context +   \\u2502\\n                                         \\u2502 answer      \\u2502\\n                                         \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                                                \\u2502\\n                                                \\u25bc\\n                                         \\u2713 PIPELINE CONTINUES\\n```\\n\\n## Component Changes\\n\\n### 1. `_execute_agent_background` Method (MODIFY)\\n\\n**Location**: `backend/main.py`, line ~165\\n\\n**Current Behavior**:\\n```python\\n# After agent execution\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"logs\\"].append(\\"\\u2705 Completed successfully\\")\\n```\\n\\n**New Behavior**:\\n```python\\n# Check for needs_user_input BEFORE marking completed\\nif result and result.get(\\"status\\") == \\"needs_user_input\\":\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"awaiting_user_input\\"\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"awaiting_question_id\\"] = result.get(\\"question_id\\")\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"continuation_context\\"] = {\\n        \\"original_input\\": input_data,\\n        \\"question\\": result.get(\\"user_question\\"),\\n        \\"agent_type\\": self.active_agents[agent_id].get(\\"type\\")\\n    }\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"logs\\"].append(f\\"\\u2753 Waiting for user input...\\")\\n    return  # DO NOT mark as completed\\nelse:\\n    # Normal completion\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\n    self.active_agents[agent_id][\\"logs\\"].append(\\"\\u2705 Completed successfully\\")\\n```\\n\\n### 2. `answer_question` Endpoint (MODIFY)\\n\\n**Location**: `backend/main.py`, line ~605\\n\\n**Current Behavior**:\\n```python\\n@app.post(\\"/api/activity/questions/{question_id}/answer\\")\\nasync def answer_question(question_id: str, answer: dict):\\n    tracker.record_answer(question_id, answer[\\"answer\\"])\\n    return {\\"success\\": True}\\n```\\n\\n**New Behavior**:\\n```python\\n@app.post(\\"/api/activity/questions/{question_id}/answer\\")\\nasync def answer_question(question_id: str, answer: dict, background_tasks: BackgroundTasks):\\n    tracker.record_answer(question_id, answer[\\"answer\\"])\\n    \\n    # Find agent waiting for this answer and trigger continuation\\n    for agent_id, agent_info in orchestrator.active_agents.items():\\n        if agent_info.get(\\"awaiting_question_id\\") == question_id:\\n            background_tasks.add_task(\\n                orchestrator.continue_agent_with_answer,\\n                agent_id,\\n                answer[\\"answer\\"]\\n            )\\n            break\\n    \\n    return {\\"success\\": True}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. New `continue_agent_with_answer` Method (ADD)\\n\\n**Location**: `backend/main.py`, add to `AgentOrchestrator` class\\n\\n```python\\ndef continue_agent_with_answer(self, agent_id: str, answer: str):\\n    \\"\\"\\"Continue agent execution after receiving user answer.\\"\\"\\"\\n    agent_info = self.active_agents.get(agent_id)\\n    if not agent_info:\\n        return\\n    \\n    context = agent_info.get(\\"continuation_context\\", {})\\n    original_input = context.get(\\"original_input\\", {})\\n    question = context.get(\\"question\\", \\"\\")\\n    \\n    # Build continuation input\\n    continuation_input = {\\n        **original_input,\\n        \\"continuation_context\\": {\\n            \\"previous_question\\": question,\\n            \\"user_answer\\": answer,\\n            \\"instruction\\": \\"Continue with implementation based on user\'s clarification.\\"\\n        }\\n    }\\n    \\n    # Spawn new executive director with continuation context\\n    # (reuse existing spawn_executive_director logic)\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n### New Fields in `active_agents[agent_id]`\\n\\n| Field | Type | Purpose |\\n|-------|------|---------|\\n| `status` | string | Now includes `\\"awaiting_user_input\\"` state |\\n| `awaiting_question_id` | string | Links agent to pending question |\\n| `continuation_context` | object | Stores context for resumption |\\n| `continuation_context.original_input` | object | Original task input |\\n| `continuation_context.question` | string | The question asked |\\n| `continuation_context.agent_type` | string | Type of agent to respawn |\\n\\n### State Transitions\\n\\n```\\ninitializing \\u2192 running \\u2192 awaiting_user_input \\u2192 [answer received] \\u2192 running \\u2192 completed\\n                                      \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 OR \\u2192 error\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n1. Test `_execute_agent_background` correctly detects `needs_user_input`\\n2. Test continuation context is properly stored\\n3. Test `continue_agent_with_answer` builds correct input\\n\\n### Integration Tests\\n1. Mock agent returns `needs_user_input` \\u2192 verify status is `awaiting_user_input`\\n2. Submit answer \\u2192 verify new agent spawned with correct context\\n3. End-to-end flow from question to continuation\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n| File | Changes |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `backend/main.py` | Main implementation - all 3 components |\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n| Risk | Mitigation |\\n|------|------------|\\n| Agent state lost on restart | Out of scope - noted as limitation |\\n| Multiple concurrent answers | Use question_id to match correctly |\\n| Original agent context stale | Copy context at pause time |\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Persistent storage for paused agents\\n- Multi-question support\\n- Question timeout handling\\n- Hot reload of agent definitions during continuation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XPWjVVkiUcYKGfsmpByC89', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '63ae09b4', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Read architecture document successfully. Task is to implement design phase pause fix in backend/main.py with 3 main components: 1) Modify _execute_agent_background to handle needs_user_input status, 2) Modify answer_question endpoint to trigger continuation, 3) Add continue_agent_with_answer method'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XPWjVVkiUcYKGfsmpByC89', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are