tivity Tracker** (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/runtime/agents/tools.py` - `WriteFileTool.execute()`\\n   - Impact: Files written by spawned agents are never tracked\\n\\n2. **Bug #2: Request Counts Never Incremented** (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n   - Method `increment_request_counts()` is defined but never called\\n   - Impact: Timeline view shows 0 agents, 0 files, 0 commits for all requests\\n\\n3. **Bug #3: File Tracking Only Scans Output Directory** (LOW PRIORITY)\\n   - Location: `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n   - Only files in output directory are scanned; files elsewhere are missed\\n   - Impact: Test files, source files written outside output directory not tracked\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Primary**: Ensure all file writes by agents are tracked via `record_file_generated()`\\n2. **Secondary**: Auto-increment request counters when agents start, files generate, commits occur\\n3. **Tertiary**: Validate fixes by confirming `/api/activity/files` returns correct data\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Modify `WriteFileTool` to accept and use tracking context (agent_id, request_id, agent_name)\\n- Modify `ToolRegistry.default()` to pass tracking context to WriteFileTool\\n- Add auto-increment calls to `record_agent_started()`, `record_file_generated()`, `record_git_commit()`\\n- Add tests to verify activity tracking works end-to-end\\n- Update existing tests if needed to accommodate new parameters\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the activity API endpoints (they already work correctly)\\n- Changing the frontend display logic (it already consumes the API correctly)\\n- Major refactoring of the tool system architecture\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Fix 1: WriteFileTool Tracking\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(self, agent_definition: Optional[\\"AgentDefinition\\"] = None):\\n        self.agent_definition = agent_definition\\n```\\n\\n**Required Changes:**\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self, \\n        agent_definition: Optional[\\"AgentDefinition\\"] = None,\\n        agent_id: Optional[str] = None,\\n        agent_name: Optional[str] = None,\\n        request_id: Optional[str] = None\\n    ):\\n        self.agent_definition = agent_definition\\n        self.agent_id = agent_id\\n        self.agent_name = agent_name or (agent_definition.name if agent_definition else \\"unknown\\")\\n        self.request_id = request_id\\n```\\n\\n**In execute() method, after successful write:**\\n```python\\nif self.agent_id and self.request_id:\\n    try:\\n        from .runtime import AgentRuntime\\n        activity_tracker = AgentRuntime.get_activity_tracker()\\n        \\n        file_ext = file_path.suffix.lower()\\n        file_type_map = {\\n            \\".md\\": \\"markdown\\", \\".py\\": \\"python\\", \\".js\\": \\"javascript\\",\\n            \\".tsx\\": \\"typescript-react\\", \\".ts\\": \\"typescript\\",\\n            \\".json\\": \\"json\\", \\".yaml\\": \\"yaml\\", \\".yml\\": \\"yaml\\", \\".txt\\": \\"text\\"\\n        }\\n        file_type = file_type_map.get(file_ext, \\"unknown\\")\\n        \\n        preview = content[:500] if len(content) > 500 else content\\n        \\n        activity_tracker.record_file_generated(\\n            agent_id=self.agent_id,\\n            agent_name=self.agent_name,\\n            request_id=self.request_id,\\n            file_path=str(file_path),\\n            file_size=len(content),\\n            file_type=file_type,\\n            preview=preview\\n        )\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        logger.warning(f\\"Failed to record file generation: {e}\\")\\n```\\n\\n### Fix 2: ToolRegistry.default() Update\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n```python\\nregistry.register(WriteFileTool(agent_definition))\\n```\\n\\n**Required Change:**\\n```python\\nregistry.register(WriteFileTool(\\n    agent_definition=agent_definition,\\n    agent_id=agent_id,\\n    agent_name=agent_definition.name if agent_definition else None,\\n    request_id=request_id\\n))\\n```\\n\\n### Fix 3: Auto-Increment Request Counts\\n\\n**In `record_agent_started()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_started(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, agents=1)\\n```\\n\\n**In `record_file_generated()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_file_generated(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, files=1)\\n```\\n\\n**In `record_git_commit()`:**\\n```python\\ndef record_git_commit(self, ...):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, commits=1)\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **File Tracking Verification:**\\n   - Run an agent workflow that creates files\\n   - Query `/api/activity/files` \\n   - Verify response includes newly created files with correct metadata\\n\\n2. **Request Counts Verification:**\\n   - Query `/api/activity/timeline`\\n   - Verify `agent_count`, `file_count`, `commit_count` are non-zero for active requests\\n\\n3. **Regression Testing:**\\n   - All existing tests pass\\n   - New tests for activity tracking pass\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n\\n1. **Unit Tests:**\\n   - Test WriteFileTool records to activity tracker when context is provided\\n   - Test WriteFileTool gracefully handles missing context (backward compatibility)\\n   - Test increment_request_counts updates counters correctly\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests:**\\n   - Test full agent execution records file generation\\n   - Test timeline API returns correct counts\\n   - Test files API returns files with correct agent attribution\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n\\n1. The ActivityTracker singleton pattern will work for capturing all file writes\\n2. Import cycle concerns can be handled with local imports\\n3. Existing API endpoints don\'t need modification - they already query the tracker correctly\\n4. Minor performance impact of tracking is acceptable\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n1. Must maintain backward compatibility - tools should work even without tracking context\\n2. Must not break existing tests\\n3. Changes should be localized to the identified files\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `src/runtime/agents/tools.py` with WriteFileTool tracking\\n2. Updated `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` with auto-increment calls\\n3. Test file(s) verifying the fix\\n4. Updated documentation (this file + any inline comments)\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Requirements documented: 2026-01-14*\\n*Project ID: 87cc4aaf*\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MpToVLnN5dta2jpeYvc2ua', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Activity Tracking Fixes - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nFix three critical bugs preventing proper activity tracking in Ensemble UI. Files, agent counts, and activity metrics are not being recorded despite agents functioning correctly.\n\n## Milestone 1: Core Activity Tracking Fix (HIGH PRIORITY)\n**Duration**: 3-4 hours\n**Objective**: Fix WriteFileTool to record file generation and auto-increment request counts\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Modified WriteFileTool** (`src/runtime/agents/tools.py`)\n   - Accept tracking context parameters (agent_id, request_id, agent_name)\n   - Call `record_file_generated()` after successful file writes\n   - Maintain backward compatibility\n\n2. **Updated ToolRegistry** (`src/runtime/agents/tools.py`)\n   - Pass tracking context to WriteFileTool in `default()` method\n\n3. **Auto-increment Request Counts** (`src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`)\n   - Add increment calls to `record_agent_started()`\n   - Add increment calls to `record_file_generated()`\n   - Add increment calls to `record_git_commit()`\n\n4. **Integration Tests**\n   - Test WriteFileTool records to ActivityTracker\n   - Test request counts increment correctly\n   - Test API endpoints return correct data\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Files generated by agents appear in `/api/activity/files`\n- Timeline view shows non-zero counts for agents, files, commits\n- All existing tests continue to pass\n- New activity tracking tests pass\n\n### Dependencies:\n- None (standalone fixes)\n\n### Technical Risks:\n- Import cycles when accessing ActivityTracker\n- Performance impact of tracking (minimal expected)\n- Backward compatibility with existing tool usage\n\n## Milestone 2: Extended File Scanning (LOW PRIORITY) \n**Duration**: 1-2 hours\n**Objective**: Scan files outside output directory for complete tracking\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Enhanced File Discovery** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`)\n   - Scan test directories, source directories\n   - Filter relevant file types\n   - Maintain performance for large codebases\n\n2. **Updated File API**\n   - Return files from multiple directories\n   - Properly categorize files by type/location\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Test files written by agents appear in activity tracking\n- Source files written outside output directory are tracked\n- No significant performance degradation\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestone 1 must be completed first\n\n## Milestone 3: Validation and Documentation\n**Duration**: 1 hour\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and documentation update\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **End-to-End Tests**\n   - Full agent workflow generates files\n   - Activity APIs return correct data\n   - Timeline shows accurate metrics\n\n2. **Documentation Updates**\n   - Update inline code comments\n   - Document activity tracking workflow\n   - Update troubleshooting guides\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Complete test coverage of activity tracking\n- Documentation accurately reflects new behavior\n- All regression tests pass\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestones 1 and 2 completed\n\n## Implementation Priority\n1. **Start with Milestone 1** - addresses the high-impact bugs\n2. **Milestone 2 can be deferred** if time constraints exist\n3. **Milestone 3 is essential** for maintainability\n\n## Success Metrics\n- `/api/activity/files` returns files created by agents\n- `/api/activity/timeline` shows non-zero counts\n- Zero regression in existing functionality\n- UI displays actual agent activity instead of empty state\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **Import cycles**: Use local imports within methods\n- **Backward compatibility**: Make tracking parameters optional\n- **Performance**: Implement efficient tracking with minimal overhead\n- **Testing**: Comprehensive unit and integration test coverage\n\n---\n*Milestone Plan Created: 2026-01-14*\n*Project: Activity Tracking Fixes*\n*Development Manager: AI Assistant*'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MpToVLnN5dta2jpeYvc2ua', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224233.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224233.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and