{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:42:36", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e7842a83-141e-4ca1-b91e-682d3783e4bd', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_families/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Families Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011JGHrRUuWkhyJhM1qbzpAY', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_families/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011JGHrRUuWkhyJhM1qbzpAY', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Families Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nImplement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups to provide visual cohesion and collective tracking across the ensemble.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n1. **Family Name Generation**\\n   - Unique family name generated when Executive Director spawns a new task group\\n   - Family name should be consistent and memorable\\n   - Supports tracking of collective achievements\\n\\n2. **Family Name Inheritance**\\n   - All child agents automatically inherit the parent\'s family name\\n   - Family name persists throughout the entire task lifecycle\\n   - Stored in agent metadata and runtime state\\n\\n3. **UI and Tracking Enhancements**\\n   - Update UI hierarchy view to display family groupings\\n   - Expose family information through API endpoints\\n   - Create visual indicators for family-based relationships\\n\\n4. **Family Achievements**\\n   - Implement at least 3 types of family-level achievements\\n   - Track collective metrics across family members\\n   - Provide aggregated performance insights\\n\\n## Technical Implementation Locations\\n- Runtime System:\\n  * `src/runtime/agents/name_generator.py`\\n  * `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n  * `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n\\n- Frontend Components:\\n  * Require updates to agent display interfaces\\n  * API endpoint modifications for family data exposure\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2713 New tasks spawn with unique, consistent family names\\n- \\u2713 Child agents automatically inherit family name\\n- \\u2713 Family names visible in all agent displays\\n- \\u2713 API supports family information retrieval\\n- \\u2713 Family-level achievement tracking implemented\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Maintain existing agent spawning mechanisms\\n- Minimal performance overhead for name generation\\n- Backwards compatibility with existing systems\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Detailed family history tracking\\n- Complex genealogy systems\\n- Permanent family assignments across multiple projects\\n\\n## Potential Family Achievement Types\\n1. Collective Task Completion\\n2. Efficiency Metrics\\n3. Innovation Score\\n4. Collaborative Problem Solving\\n\\n## Notes\\n- Use whimsical, memorable naming strategies\\n- Ensure randomness prevents predictable family names\\n- Design for extensibility of family concept"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NCsdJBFSAZwCvWNaiHaDdB', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Agent Families Implementation Milestones\n\n## Milestone 1: Name Generation and Runtime Integration\n- Objective: Implement core family name generation and runtime inheritance\n- Deliverables:\n  * Updated name generation logic\n  * Runtime metadata enhancement\n  * Basic family name tracking\n- Acceptance Criteria:\n  * Unique family names generated\n  * Family names inherited by child agents\n  * Minimal performance impact\n\n## Milestone 2: UI and API Enhancements\n- Objective: Update frontend displays and API endpoints\n- Deliverables:\n  * Family grouping visualization\n  * API endpoint modifications\n  * Frontend component updates\n- Acceptance Criteria:\n  * Family names visible in agent displays\n  * Family information retrievable via API\n\n## Milestone 3: Achievement Tracking\n- Objective: Implement family-level achievement tracking\n- Deliverables:\n  * Achievement type definitions\n  * Tracking mechanisms\n  * Aggregation and reporting logic\n- Acceptance Criteria:\n  * 3+ achievement types implemented\n  * Collective metrics tracked\n  * Performance insights generated'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NCsdJBFSAZwCvWNaiHaDdB', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224236.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224236.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose