xecutive_director", "note": "Project \'Logs Agents Tab Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XbgWDRLpiyyBLvrw3Ec2kn', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/logs_agents_tab/milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XbgWDRLpiyyBLvrw3Ec2kn', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Backend Logs Tab & Agent Definition Explorer\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nAdd a new \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab to the Ensemble UI with:\\n1. Real-time backend log streaming\\n2. Agent definition file explorer with view/edit capabilities\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n- **WebSocket for log streaming**: Leverage existing WebSocket infrastructure (already have `/ws/agent-status`)\\n- **React Bootstrap for UI**: Match existing UI framework\\n- **Simple textarea for editing**: No need for Monaco editor initially (per requirements)\\n- **Existing API endpoints**: Leverage `/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`\\n- **Split-pane layout**: Use CSS flexbox for responsive split pane\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Backend Log Streaming Infrastructure\\n**Objective**: Create WebSocket endpoint and log buffer for real-time log streaming\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Log buffer class with size-limited ring buffer (1000 entries)\\n2. WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for log streaming\\n3. Log filtering by level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n4. Log filtering by agent_id and request_id\\n5. Structured log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] WebSocket endpoint accepts connections and streams logs\\n- [ ] Log buffer doesn\'t exceed 1000 entries (memory safety)\\n- [ ] Logs include structured metadata (agent_id, request_id, timestamp, level)\\n- [ ] Filtering works on server-side before sending to client\\n- [ ] Existing logging continues to work (no performance degradation)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (foundational milestone)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Log Viewer Component\\n**Objective**: Create React component to display streamed logs\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `LogStreamPanel.jsx` component\\n2. WebSocket connection to `/ws/logs`\\n3. Auto-scroll with toggle\\n4. Log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n5. Search filter for agent_id/request_id\\n6. Pause/Resume streaming\\n7. Clear logs button\\n8. Color coding by log level\\n9. Timestamp display (relative/absolute toggle)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Component connects to WebSocket and displays logs\\n- [ ] Auto-scroll works and can be toggled\\n- [ ] Filters work correctly (level, search)\\n- [ ] Pause/Resume controls work\\n- [ ] Clear button clears displayed logs\\n- [ ] Color coding matches log levels\\n- [ ] Timestamps are readable\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (backend log streaming)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Agent Definition Explorer Component\\n**Objective**: Create tree-view file explorer for agent definitions\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `AgentExplorer.jsx` component\\n2. Tree-view with collapsible directories\\n3. Integration with existing `/api/agents` endpoint\\n4. Directory structure: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\\n5. Click to select agent file\\n6. Visual indicators for selected file\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Tree displays all agent directories correctly\\n- [ ] Directories can be expanded/collapsed\\n- [ ] Clicking a file selects it\\n- [ ] Visual feedback for selection state\\n- [ ] Icons differentiate files and folders\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (can run in parallel with Milestone 2)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Agent Definition Viewer/Editor\\n**Objective**: Create component to view and edit agent definitions\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `AgentDefinitionViewer.jsx` component\\n2. Read-only view mode (default)\\n3. Edit mode with toggle\\n4. Textarea for editing content\\n5. Markdown preview panel\\n6. Save button with confirmation\\n7. Revert functionality (from backup)\\n8. Success/error feedback\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] View mode displays file content\\n- [ ] Edit toggle switches to editable textarea\\n- [ ] Save calls `/api/agents/update` endpoint\\n- [ ] Success message shows backup path\\n- [ ] Revert option works\\n- [ ] Error handling for failed saves\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 3 (explorer provides file selection)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 5: Tab Integration & Final Assembly\\n**Objective**: Integrate components into new tab in App.jsx\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Tab navigation component in App.jsx\\n2. \\"Main View\\" tab (existing content)\\n3. \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab (new content)\\n4. Split-pane layout in new tab\\n5. Responsive design\\n6. State management for tab switching\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Tab navigation works smoothly\\n- [ ] Existing functionality preserved in \\"Main View\\"\\n- [ ] New tab shows logs panel + agent explorer/editor\\n- [ ] Split pane is resizable or has good default split\\n- [ ] UI follows existing dark theme\\n- [ ] All components integrate correctly\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 2, 3, 4 (all components ready)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Milestone 1: ~2 hours (backend)\\n- Milestone 2: ~3 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 3: ~2 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 4: ~3 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 5: ~2 hours (integration)\\n\\n**Total**: ~12 hours of development work\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n1. **Low Risk**: WebSocket infrastructure exists, just adding another endpoint\\n2. **Low Risk**: API endpoints for agents already exist\\n3. **Medium Risk**: Tab integration might need CSS adjustments for layout\\n4. **Low Risk**: React Bootstrap components are well-documented\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\\n2. Users can browse all agent definition files in tree structure\\n3. Users can view and edit agent definitions with backup\\n4. Log streaming doesn\'t degrade backend performance\\n5. UI matches existing design patterns\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EiGgXMMgAFiFi9pS4CoxAJ', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'f09c84d5', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': "Requirements document read successfully. Project involves adding a new 'Logs & Agents' tab to Ensemble UI with real-time backend log streaming and agent definition file explorer. 5 milestones identified with ~12 hours estimated development work."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EiGgXMMgAFiFi9pS4CoxAJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GSzKPqZb5sLpbXSGVRXyFC', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Requirements Document: Logs & Agents Tab Implementation\n\n## Project Vision\nImplement a comprehensive "Logs & Agents" tab for the Ensemble UI that provides real-time backend log monitoring and agent definition file management capabilities. This will enable users to monitor system behavior in real-time and manage agent configurations through a user-friendly interface.\n\n## Core Objectives\n1. **Real-time Log Streaming**: Enable users to view backend logs as they happen\n2. **Agent File Management**: Provide a file explorer for viewing and editing agent definitions\n3. **Seamless Integration**: Add new functionality without disrupting existing UI\n4. **Performance Safety**: Ensure log streaming doesn\'t degrade system performance\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### F1: Backend Log Streaming\n- **F1.1**: Create WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for real-time log streaming\n- **F1.2**: Implement log buffer with 1000-entry limit for memory safety\n- **F1.3**: Structure log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\n- **F1.4**: Support server-side filtering by log level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\n- **F1.5**: Support server-side filtering by agent_id and request_id\n- **F1.6**: Maintain existing logging functionality without performance degradation\n\n### F2: Frontend Log Viewer\n- **F2.1**: Create LogStreamPanel component with WebSocket connection\n- **F2.2**: Implement auto-scroll with toggle functionality\n- **F2.3**: Provide log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\n- **F2.4**: Include search filter for agent_id/request_id\n- **F2.5**: Support pause/resume streaming controls\n- **F2.6**: Provide clear logs functionality\n- **F2.7**: Implement color coding by log level\n- **F2.8**: Display timestamps with relative/absolute toggle\n\n### F3: Agent Definition Explorer\n- **F3.1**: Create AgentExplorer component with tree-view structure\n- **F3.2**: Display directories: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\n- **F3.3**: Support collapsible/expandable directories\n- **F3.4**: Enable file selection with visual feedback\n- **F3.5**: Use existing `/api/agents` endpoint for data\n- **F3.6**: Differentiate files and folders with appropriate icons\n\n### F4: Agent Definition Editor\n- **F4.1**: Create AgentDefinitionViewer component with read-only default view\n- **F4.2**: Implement edit mode toggle with textarea editing\n- **F4.3**: Provide markdown preview panel\n- **F4.4**: Integrate with existing `/api/agents/update` endpoint for saving\n- **F4.5**: Implement automatic backup functionality\n- **F4.6**: Provide revert functionality using backups\n- **F4.7**: Display success/error feedback for save operations\n\n### F5: Tab Integration\n- **F5.1**: Add tab navigation to App.jsx with "Main View" and "Logs & Agents" tabs\n- **F5.2**: Preserve all existing functionality in "Main View" tab\n- **F5.3**: Implement split-pane layout in "Logs & Agents" tab\n- **F5.4**: Ensure responsive design across screen sizes\n- **F5.5**: Maintain consistent dark theme styling\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### NF1: Performance\n- Log streaming must not degrade backend performance\n- WebSocket connections should be efficiently managed\n- Log buffer must not exceed memory constraints (1000 entries)\n\n### NF2: Usability\n- UI must follow existing design patterns and dark theme\n- Components must be responsive across different screen sizes\n- Interface should be intuitive for developers and administrators\n\n### NF3: Reliability\n- WebSocket connections should handle disconnections gracefully\n- File editing should include backup/recovery mechanisms\n- Error states should be clearly communicated to users\n\n### NF4: Maintainability\n- Code should follow existing project conventions\n- Components should be modular and reusable\n- TDD methodology must be followed (tests before implementation)\n\n## Technical Constraints\n- Must use existing WebSocket infrastructure (building on `/ws/agent-status`)\n- Must use React Bootstrap for UI consistency\n- Must integrate with existing API endpoints (`/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`)\n- Must use simple textarea for editing (no Monaco editor requirement)\n- Must use CSS flexbox for split-pane layout\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\n2. Log streaming includes filtering by level and search terms\n3. Users can browse agent definition files in intuitive tree structure\n4. Users can view and edit agent definitions with automatic backup\n5. Tab integration preserves existing functionality\n6. System performance remains stable under normal log volume\n7. All tests pass (following TDD methodology)\n8. UI maintains consistency with existing design\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Advanced log analysis or aggregation features\n- Complex code editing features (syntax highlighting, IntelliSense)\n- User authentication/authorization for file editing\n- Log persistence to database\n- Advanced layout customization options\n\n## Dependencies\n- Existing WebSocket infrastructure (`/ws/agent-status`)\n- Existing agent API endpoints\n- React Bootstrap framework\n- Current dark theme CSS\n\n## Assumptions Made\n- Standard log volumes won\'t exceed buffer capacity under normal operation\n- Users have appropriate permissions for file system access\n- Existing API endpoints provide sufficient data for agent management\n- WebSocket infrastructure can handle additional concurrent connections\n- Current UI framework (React Bootstrap) is sufficient for new components\n\n## Testing Requirements\nFollowing TDD methodology:\n1. Unit tests for all React components\n2. Integration tests for WebSocket connections\n3. API integration tests for agent management\n4. End-to-end tests for complete user workflows\n5. Performance tests for log streaming under load'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GSzKPqZb5sLpbXSGVRXyFC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224231.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224231.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XzYwAZ6JBsk96jVGakTRDU', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'f09c84d5', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements document completed and written to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md. Ready to delegate to Development Manager for implementation.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XzYwAZ6JBsk96jVGakTRDU', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01G6vPJM8xnYKXkzhcAE9SGf', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'f09c84d5', 'description': 'Implement Logs & Agents Tab features including backend log streaming infrastructure, frontend log viewer, agent definition explorer, and tab integration following TDD methodology', 'assigned_to': 'leadership/development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01G6vPJM8xnYKXkzhcAE9SGf', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "bbcd1fa9", "message": "Added task: Implement Logs & Agents Tab features including backend log streaming infrastructure, frontend log viewer, agent definition explorer, and tab integration following TDD methodology"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 76.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
