{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:42:46", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-ab97f235-90d5-4cb5-bbf5-b2c4f976bf85', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_families/architecture.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BoKwgJNoaCNSkb3cZpezTU', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Families Implementation', 'description': 'Implement the requirements documented in agent_families/architecture.md following TDD methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BoKwgJNoaCNSkb3cZpezTU', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "2a974de4", "message": "Created project: Agent Families Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "2a974de4", "project_name": "Agent Families Implementation", "description": "Implement the requirements documented in agent_families/architecture.md following TDD methodology", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:21.749481", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:21.749481", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:42:21.749481", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Families Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01He9biuNt1NhP16YjQ5ytnU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_families/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01He9biuNt1NhP16YjQ5ytnU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Families Implementation - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Layered Modular Architecture\\nThe Agent Families system will be implemented using a layered, modular architecture that ensures:\\n- Clear separation of concerns\\n- Extensibility for future family-related features\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Backwards compatibility\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Runtime**: Existing agent runtime system\\n- **Libraries**: \\n  - `uuid` for unique identifier generation\\n  - `functools` for memoization and performance optimization\\n- **Performance Considerations**: \\n  - Lightweight name generation\\n  - Minimal additional runtime state storage\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: Existing React-based UI\\n- **State Management**: Existing Context API or Redux\\n- **Visualization**: D3.js for relationship graph enhancements\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Family Name Generator (`name_generator.py`)\\n- Responsible for generating unique, memorable family names\\n- Key Methods:\\n  ```python\\n  def generate_family_name() -> str:\\n      # Generates a unique, whimsical family name\\n      # Ensures randomness and memorability\\n  \\n  def validate_family_name(name: str) -> bool:\\n      # Checks name uniqueness and naming rules\\n  ```\\n\\n### 2. Family Tracker (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n- Manages family-level metrics and achievements\\n- Tracks collective performance\\n- Key Methods:\\n  ```python\\n  def record_family_achievement(family_name: str, achievement_type: str):\\n      # Record achievement for entire family\\n  \\n  def get_family_metrics(family_name: str) -> Dict:\\n      # Retrieve aggregated family performance\\n  ```\\n\\n### 3. Runtime Integration (`runtime.py`)\\n- Modify existing agent spawning mechanism\\n- Implement family name inheritance\\n- Extend agent metadata\\n\\n### 4. Frontend Components\\n- Family Name Display Module\\n- Family Achievement Visualization\\n- API Integration Layer\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 name_generator.py     # Family name generation logic\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 activity_tracker.py   # Family achievement tracking\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 runtime.py            # Runtime modifications\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 interfaces/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 family_api.py         # API endpoint definitions\\n\\nfrontend/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FamilyNameDisplay.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 FamilyAchievementGraph.tsx\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useFamilyMetrics.ts\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Family Metadata Structure\\n```python\\nclass FamilyMetadata:\\n    name: str              # Unique family identifier\\n    creation_timestamp: datetime\\n    achievements: List[Dict]\\n    members: List[AgentID]\\n    metrics: Dict[str, float]\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### New Endpoints\\n- `GET /families`: List all current families\\n- `GET /family/{family_name}`: Get family details\\n- `GET /family/{family_name}/achievements`: Retrieve family achievements\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n- Deploy as part of existing agent runtime\\n- No additional infrastructure required\\n- Minimal configuration changes\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n- Name generation randomness\\n- Family name validation\\n- Achievement tracking accuracy\\n\\n### Integration Tests\\n- Family inheritance during agent spawning\\n- API endpoint functionality\\n- UI component rendering\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Complex Genealogy System\\n- **Pros**: More detailed tracking\\n- **Cons**: Significant complexity, performance overhead\\n- **Decision**: Rejected in favor of lightweight approach\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Static Family Names\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Less dynamic, reduced memorability\\n- **Decision**: Rejected; dynamic generation preferred\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - *Mitigation*: Lightweight name generation, memoization\\n   \\n2. **Name Collision**\\n   - *Mitigation*: Robust uniqueness checking, retry mechanism\\n\\n3. **UI Integration Complexity**\\n   - *Mitigation*: Incremental UI updates, clear component interfaces\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n- Exact naming strategy for family names\\n- Specific achievement type implementations\\n- Performance testing thresholds\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nThis architecture provides a flexible, performant solution for implementing Agent Families with minimal system disruption."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015AvQfkRGJVdqM2qztHyR1x', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '2a974de4', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements document successfully read from agent_families/architecture.md. Document contains comprehensive specifications for Agent Families implementation with 4 main components: name generator, activity tracker, runtime integration, and frontend components.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015AvQfkRGJVdqM2qztHyR1x', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MHBUhhiHqGs8iUvZbWC2sh', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Agent Families Implementation - Requirements Document\n\n## Project Vision\nImplement the Agent Families feature as specified in the architecture document to provide:\n- Unique, memorable family names for agent hierarchies\n- Family-level performance tracking and achievements\n- Enhanced UI visualization of agent relationships\n- Lightweight integration with existing agent runtime\n\n## Core Objectives\n1. **Family Name Generation**: Create unique, whimsical family names for agent spawning trees\n2. **Family Achievement Tracking**: Monitor and record collective performance metrics\n3. **Runtime Integration**: Seamlessly integrate family metadata into existing agent spawning\n4. **UI Enhancements**: Visualize family relationships and achievements in the frontend\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR1: Family Name Generator\n- Generate unique, memorable family names using whimsical adjective + animal combinations\n- Ensure name uniqueness across all active families\n- Provide validation for family name format and rules\n- Support retry mechanism for collision handling\n\n### FR2: Family Activity Tracker\n- Record family-level achievements and metrics\n- Track collective performance across family members\n- Store achievement timestamps and types\n- Provide aggregated family performance data\n\n### FR3: Runtime Integration\n- Modify agent spawning to inherit family names from parent agents\n- Extend agent metadata to include family information\n- Maintain backwards compatibility with existing agent creation\n- Ensure minimal performance overhead\n\n### FR4: Frontend Components\n- Display family names in agent UI\n- Visualize family achievement graphs\n- Provide family metrics dashboard\n- Integrate with existing React-based interface\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n### Backend Implementation\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Files to implement**:\n  - `src/runtime/agents/name_generator.py`\n  - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` \n  - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` (modifications)\n  - `src/runtime/interfaces/family_api.py`\n\n### Frontend Implementation\n- **Framework**: React/TypeScript\n- **Files to implement**:\n  - `frontend/components/FamilyNameDisplay.tsx`\n  - `frontend/components/FamilyAchievementGraph.tsx`\n  - `frontend/hooks/useFamilyMetrics.ts`\n\n### API Endpoints\n- `GET /families` - List all current families\n- `GET /family/{family_name}` - Get family details\n- `GET /family/{family_name}/achievements` - Retrieve family achievements\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### Performance\n- Family name generation must complete within 100ms\n- Family tracking overhead must be < 5% of agent spawning time\n- UI updates must render within 200ms\n\n### Reliability\n- 99.9% uptime for family tracking\n- Zero data loss for family achievements\n- Graceful degradation if family features fail\n\n### Compatibility\n- Maintain full backwards compatibility with existing agent system\n- Support existing agent metadata structure\n- No breaking changes to current API\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. Family names are generated and displayed for all new agent spawning trees\n2. Family achievements are tracked and visible in UI\n3. All existing agent functionality remains unchanged\n4. Test coverage > 90% for new family-related code\n5. Performance benchmarks met for name generation and tracking\n\n## Assumptions Made\n- Using existing React/TypeScript frontend stack\n- Python backend with existing runtime system\n- D3.js available for graph visualization\n- Standard REST API patterns for new endpoints\n- TDD methodology with comprehensive test coverage\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Complex genealogy tracking beyond parent-child relationships\n- Historical family data migration\n- Advanced analytics or reporting features\n- Third-party integrations\n- Custom family name creation by users\n\n## Constraints\n- Must not modify existing database schema\n- Cannot break existing agent spawning workflows\n- Limited to read-only family name generation (no user customization)\n- Must work within existing authentication/authorization system\n\n## Dependencies\n- Existing agent runtime system\n- React frontend framework\n- Current API infrastructure\n- Agent metadata storage system'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MHBUhhiHqGs8iUvZbWC2sh', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224246.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224246.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 76.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed effici